[size=5][b]⚔ For modders[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Hybrid weapons for modders[/b][/size]

Your own weapons can work the way katars and knuckledusters do - or be a different kind of hybrid: a mace that trains Blunt Weapon and Destruction, a spear only as good as the weaker of Spear and Conjuration. No scripting needed. Make the weapons in your plugin as usual, and next to it ship one small file per weapon in a [font=Courier New]HybridWeaponDefinitions[/font] folder, named after the weapon's record id:

[code]Data Files/
  MyMod.esp
  HybridWeaponDefinitions/
    my_flame_mace.yaml[/code]

[code]# HybridWeaponDefinitions/my_flame_mace.yaml
primarySkill: handtohand
secondarySkill: destruction
primaryExperience: 0.7
secondaryExperience: 0.5
scaling: lowestSkill
moveset: default
tooltip: "Battlemage's mace: as effective as the lower of %{primarySkill} (%{primary}) and %{secondarySkill} (%{secondary})."[/code]

YAML or JSON ([font=Courier New].yaml[/font], [font=Courier New].yml[/font], [font=Courier New].json[/font]). Only melee weapons can be hybrids. The record's weapon type stays what the engine sees - handedness, reach, damage - and whichever skill that type uses is the one the mod stands in for: on every swing it's set to what the hybrid's skills make, then set back, and on every hit its experience is handed out by the shares below.

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]primarySkill[/font] (required) - a skill id: [font=Courier New]handtohand[/font], [font=Courier New]shortblade[/font], [font=Courier New]bluntweapon[/font], [font=Courier New]destruction[/font]... Any spelling works: [font=Courier New]Hand to Hand[/font].
[*][font=Courier New]secondarySkill[/font] (required) - a different skill.
[*][font=Courier New]primaryExperience[/font] (default [font=Courier New]0.7[/font]) - share of a successful hit's experience for the primary skill: [font=Courier New]0.7[/font] or [font=Courier New]70%[/font].
[*][font=Courier New]secondaryExperience[/font] (default [font=Courier New]0.3[/font]) - the same for the secondary skill.
[*][font=Courier New]scaling[/font] (default [font=Courier New]minorSecondaryBonus[/font]) - what a swing rolls with: [font=Courier New]minorSecondaryBonus[/font] is the primary skill plus 15% of the secondary, tapering to 5% as the secondary falls more than 10 points behind, [font=Courier New]lowestSkill[/font] the lower of the two, [font=Courier New]highestSkill[/font] the higher.
[*][font=Courier New]moveset[/font] (default [font=Courier New]default[/font]) - [font=Courier New]handToHand[/font]: this mod's fist animations, a copy of the weapon in the off hand and nothing else in that hand (one-handed weapons only). [font=Courier New]default[/font]: the weapon's own animations.
[*][font=Courier New]fatigueDamage[/font] (default [font=Courier New]0[/font]) - fatigue damage per hit, as a share of a bare-fisted punch's. Katars [font=Courier New]0.5[/font], knuckledusters [font=Courier New]0.75[/font].
[*][font=Courier New]silentDraw[/font] (default [font=Courier New]false[/font]) - no draw and sheathe sound, like bare hands.
[*][font=Courier New]swingSounds[/font] (default: the weapon's own) - swing whooshes, with Combat Sounds Overhaul Overhauled (below).
[*][font=Courier New]tooltip[/font] (default: one for its scaling) - the footnote in Inventory Extender's tooltip (placeholders below).
[/list]

A skill that isn't the weapon's own gets its share as one use of that skill - for a magic school, one successful cast. The weapon's own skill, if it's neither of the two, gets nothing.

[b]Tooltip placeholders[/b]: [font=Courier New]%{primarySkill}[/font] and [font=Courier New]%{secondarySkill}[/font] (their names), [font=Courier New]%{primary}[/font] and [font=Courier New]%{secondary}[/font] (the player's values), [font=Courier New]%{effective}[/font] (what a swing rolls with), [font=Courier New]%{bonus}[/font] (that minus the primary, as [font=Courier New]+3[/font]), [font=Courier New]%{lowest}[/font], [font=Courier New]%{highest}[/font], [font=Courier New]%{weaponSkill}[/font] (the skill the engine thinks it is), [font=Courier New]%{primaryExperience}[/font] and [font=Courier New]%{secondaryExperience}[/font] (as [font=Courier New]70%[/font]).

[b]Swing sounds[/b] are a list, one whoosh per entry, all played on every swing. [font=Courier New]sound[/font] is [font=Courier New]own[/font] - the weapon's own whoosh, from Combat Sounds Overhaul Overhauled's swing [font=Courier New]groups[/font] if you give some - or one of that mod's weapon kinds ([font=Courier New]HandToHand[/font], [font=Courier New]ShortBlade[/font], [font=Courier New]Blunt[/font], [font=Courier New]Axe[/font]...). [font=Courier New]HandToHand[/font] is the vanilla whoosh a bare fist swings with. Leave [font=Courier New]own[/font] out and the weapon's own whoosh is silent. A katar's:

[code]swingSounds:
  - sound: HandToHand
    volume: 1
  - sound: own
    volume: 0.85
    groups: [sharpMetal][/code]

Good to know:

[list]
[*]This mod's own definitions are in its [font=Courier New]HybridWeaponDefinitions[/font] folder, for reference. A file at the same path in a mod loaded later replaces this mod's, which is also how to change its weapons.
[*]A copy of a hybrid made in game - say, one the player enchanted - is recognised by its mesh and type.
[*]What's wrong with a file goes to [font=Courier New]openmw.log[/font] when a game is loaded, on lines starting [font=Courier New][H2HWeapons][/font].
[*]NPCs swing hybrids with the skill the engine gives them; the skill swap and the experience are the player's.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Scripts and source[/b][/size]

Scripts can ask about hybrids through [font=Courier New]I.H2HWeapons[/font] (in player scripts): [font=Courier New]hybridOfId(recordId)[/font], [font=Courier New]hybridOfItem(item)[/font] and [font=Courier New]equippedHybrid()[/font] give a weapon's definition, or [font=Courier New]false[/font]. How everything works - and how to build the plugin, meshes and animations from source - is written up in the [url=https://github.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/blob/main/Sources/DEVELOPMENT.md]technical notes[/url] in the git repository.
